  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="233d0c3d-c537-57c8-bff4-d2fa36ed4916" activityNameId="846746a4-959c-5e8c-8007-82807d4019d6" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Battery, NiMH, rechargeable, prismatic, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Battery, NiMH, rechargeable, prismatic, at plant
The functional unit represents 1 kg of a NiMH battery for laptop applications. A typical such NiMH battery has a weight of 0.591 kg. Process data is taken mainly from an environmental report of a battery producer as well as from literature. In addition own measurements of sizes and weights of batteries were used.;
Synonyms: NiMN-Akku; 
UUID: 723d1c56-48e0-3f09-8d14-cb966ce26939
(Raw) materials, infrastructure, transport efforts, energy consumption and waste disposal for the production of a NiMH battery. No emissions to air or water are taken into account.
Location: This module relates to the global situation (electricity consumption according to the main producing countries).
Technology: Construction details as described for NiMH-rechargable batteries and manufacturing conditions as documented in the environmental report were adopted.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 183?000 t in 2005 (own calculations)
Sampling: Literature, measurements 
Extrapolations: see technology &amp; general comments
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_723d1c56-48e0-3f09-8d14-cb966ce26939.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="f4808887-5a57-5892-975e-ba0565a93e23" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
